{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You shall not make for yourselves elilim</b> — The verse speaks concerning the one sold to a gentile, lest he say: since my master worships idolatry, I too will worship idolatry; since my master commits forbidden sexual relations, I too will commit forbidden sexual relations; since my master profanes the Sabbath, I too will profane the Sabbath. Therefore Scripture says: 'You shall not make for yourselves elilim, you shall keep My Sabbaths and revere My sanctuary' — Scripture issued warning here concerning all the commandments. This is the language of Torat Kohanim (chapter 9, halakhah 6).\n\nIts meaning is that Scripture mentioned idolatry and the Sabbath — that the servant sold to a gentile must take care concerning them — and the reverence of the sanctuary, that he should come there on the festivals and revere it; and the same reasoning applies to all the commandments. But it mentioned these specifically because they are categories that teach about all of them.\n\nThere are those whose reading is 'he mentioned here' [instead of 'he warned here'], and if the reading is thus, they hinted that all the commandments are included within the Sabbath and the sanctuary, and the enlightened will understand."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:00:52.062481952Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}